---
description: Use the managed local Graphify graph for structural code questions when it exists.
alwaysApply: true
---

For structural codebase questions, consult an existing `.tkstack/graphify/graph.json`
through the `graphify` skill or `graphify-local` MCP connection. Use query/path/
explain results to locate relevant source; verify current code and keep inferred
relationships distinct from extracted edges. An absent or stale graph is missing
context, not permission to invent relationships or automatically rebuild it.

The skill selects tkstack's pinned local runtime and keeps graph/cache state in
`.tkstack/`. Provider/model calls, semantic media extraction, watching, publication,
and delegation retain the current task's explicit scope. Code-only extraction is
available without model credentials. Keep session evidence under
`.tkstack/sessions/<session>/`. Current instructions retain precedence.
